                        Updated: <b class="text-slate-700">Oct 20, 2026</b><br />Sources: CFPB, Experian, Equifax
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Key Takeaways -->
                <div class="mt-8 rounded-[16px] bg-slate-900 text-white p-6">
                    <div class="text-[13px] tracking-widest font-bold opacity-60">KEY TAKEAWAYS • US FOCUS</div>
                    <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-[14px] leading-6 text-slate-200 !list-none !pl-0">
                        <li>✓ <b class="text-white">No annual fee, no interest, no credit check</b> — approval odds ~98% if you qualify for Chime Checking</li>
                        <li>✓ <b class="text-white">Reports to all 3 bureaus:</b> Experian, Equifax, TransUnion — critical per CFPB for building FICO</li>
                        <li>✓ <b class="text-white">Secured by your own money:</b> you move money to Credit Builder, spend up to that amount, Chime auto-pays on time</li>
                        <li>✕ <b class="text-white">Requires Chime ecosystem:</b> Chime Checking Account + $200 qualifying direct deposit to unlock</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <h2>What Is Chime Credit Builder?</h2>
                <p>Chime is a US financial technology company, not a bank. Banking services provided by The Bancorp Bank, N.A. or Stride Bank, N.A. The <b>Chime Credit Builder Visa® Secured Credit Card</b> is a secured charge card designed to help Americans with no credit or bad credit build credit history without the fees that CFPB has flagged as predatory.</p>
                <p>Unlike traditional secured cards that charge 20%+ APR and annual fees, Chime Credit Builder has <b>no annual fee, no interest, no late fees, and no credit check to apply</b>. You don't need a Social Security Number to check eligibility? Actually to open Chime you DO need an SSN for identity verification under US law, but Chime does not pull your credit to decide approval for Credit Builder — that's why approval odds are ~98%. If you have an ITIN only, you cannot open Chime today.</p>
                <p>As of 2026, over 8 million members use Credit Builder according to Chime's US public reports. It reports payment history to Experian, Equifax, and TransUnion monthly, which matches CFPB guidance that consistent on-time payment reporting to all three bureaus is the fastest way to establish a FICO Score.</p>

                <h2>How It Works: Step-by-Step</h2>
                <p>Chime designed this to solve utilization and on-time payment problems that Experian says drive 65% of your FICO.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><b>1. Open Chime Checking:</b> Download app, open fee-free Checking Account. No minimum balance in US.</li>
                    <li><b>2. Set up direct deposit:</b> You need a single qualifying direct deposit of $200 or more from employer, payroll, or benefits to be eligible for Credit Builder.</li>
                    <li><b>3. Move money to Credit Builder:</b> Transfer dollars from Checking to your secured account. This amount is your spending limit — e.g., move $500, you can spend up to $500. This is not a credit limit increase; it's your own money.</li>
                    <li><b>4. Use card for everyday purchases:</b> Use anywhere Visa is accepted in the US. Do NOT exceed your secured balance.</li>
                    <li><b>5. Safer Credit Building™:</b> Enable automatic payments. Chime automatically pays your balance on time each month using your secured balance. No due date to miss. Credit Builder carries no interest because you pay in full.</li>
                    <li><b>6. Reports to bureaus:</b> Chime reports your on-time payments to Experian, Equifax, and TransUnion. Positive payment history can build score over time per Equifax.</li>
                </ul>

                <h2>Fees: Truly $0?</h2>
                <p>We verified against CFPB complaint database and Chime disclosure:</p>
                <div class="rounded-xl border bg-white p-5 grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 text-[13px]">
                    <div><div class="text-slate-500">Annual Fee</div><div class="font-bold text-lg">$0</div></div>
                    <div><div class="text-slate-500">Interest / APR</div><div class="font-bold text-lg">0% — No interest</div></div>
                    <div><div class="text-slate-500">Credit Check to Apply</div><div class="font-bold text-lg">No hard pull</div></div>
                    <div><div class="text-slate-500">Late / Foreign Fee</div><div class="font-bold text-lg">$0</div></div>
                </div>
                <p class="mt-3 text-[12px]">There are optional fees for out-of-network ATMs or instant transfers, but not for the Credit Builder card itself. Chime is a member of the Visa network. No minimum credit score required in US.</p>

                <h2>Pros and Cons for US Consumers</h2>
                <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-5 not-prose">
                    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-emerald-100 bg-emerald-50 p-5">
                        <div class="font-bold text-emerald-900">Pros</div>
                        <ul class="mt-3 text-[13px] leading-6 text-emerald-900 space-y-2 list-disc pl-5">
                            <li>No fees that CFPB warns about: no annual, late, interest</li>
                            <li>98% approval odds if you qualify for Chime Checking (no credit score needed)</li>
                            <li>Reports to all 3 bureaus — Experian, Equifax, TransUnion — unlike many fintechs</li>
                            <li>Autopay prevents missed payments — #1 factor per Equifax</li>
                            <li>Secured balance controls spending — helps keep utilization low per Experian (under 30% recommended)</li>
                            <li>No SSN hard pull; does not hurt score to apply</li>
                            <li>Free FICO-style score tracking in Chime app</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-5">
                        <div class="font-bold">Cons</div>
                        <ul class="mt-3 text-[13px] leading-6 text-slate-600 space-y-2 list-disc pl-5">
                            <li>Requires Chime Checking + $200 direct deposit — locked into ecosystem</li>
                            <li>Not a traditional credit card — no rewards, no cashback in US</li>
                            <li>Cannot increase limit beyond what you deposit; no free credit</li>
                            <li>No upgrade path to unsecured Visa; you keep secured mechanism</li>
                            <li>Must use Chime app; no branch support in US</li>
                            <li>Does not report credit limit, so utilization calculation may differ vs Experian guidance</li>
                            <li>Requires US residency and SSN for Chime account opening</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <h2>Who Should Use It?</h2>
                <p>This card is ideal for specific US profiles, per CFPB financial coaching guidelines:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><b>College students & Gen Z:</b> From 0 credit to first score in 30-60 days. No credit check means no denial from thin file.</li>
                    <li><b>New to US / ITIN holders? No:</b> Chime requires SSN. Recent immigrants with SSN and thin file can benefit, ITIN-only cannot.</li>
                    <li><b>Rebuilders with poor history:</b> If you had late payments, secured autopay helps rebuild on-time streak. Equifax notes 12 months of on-time payments strongly improves score.</li>
                    <li><b>Avoid if you want rewards/travel:</b> Choose a traditional secured card from our <a href="/Pages/CreditCards" class="font-bold underline">Credit Cards</a> list if you need cashback.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>Methodology: ScoreUp rated this using 5 factors: fees (40%), bureau reporting (25%), approval accessibility (15%), user controls like Safer Credit Building (15%), and CFPB complaint ratio (5%). Data sourced from CFPB, Experian, Equifax public docs as of Oct 2026. This is not financial advice.</p>

                <h2>Chime vs Other No-Credit-Check Options</h2>
                <p>Many US consumers compare Chime with Self and other fintechs. Key difference: Chime is free and daily-use card; Self is an installment loan that locks savings. Both report to all 3 bureaus. For fastest FICO growth, Experian says mix of revolving (like Chime) + installment (like Self) is optimal. Try our simulator below.</p>

                <h2>FAQs — US Edition</h2>
                <div class="space-y-4 not-prose">
                    <div class="rounded-xl border p-5"><div class="font-bold text-[15px]">Does Chime Credit Builder require a credit check?</div><div class="text-[13px] text-slate-600 mt-2 leading-6">No. Chime does not perform a hard credit inquiry for Credit Builder. You still need ID verification (SSN) for the Checking account under US banking law, but your credit score is not checked. That's why approval odds are ~98% if you meet the $200 direct deposit requirement.</div></div>
                    <div class="rounded-xl border p-5"><div class="font-bold text-[15px]">Does Chime report to all 3 credit bureaus?</div><div class="text-[13px] text-slate-600 mt-2 leading-6">Yes. As of 2026, Chime Credit Builder reports to Experian, Equifax, and TransUnion monthly. This is critical — CFPB and Equifax advise that cards reporting to only 1 bureau give limited benefit.</div></div>
                    <div class="rounded-xl border p-5"><div class="font-bold text-[15px]">Can I use Chime with no SSN?</div><div class="text-[13px] text-slate-600 mt-2 leading-6">You need a valid US SSN to open a Chime Checking Account. Chime does not currently accept ITIN only. Without SSN you cannot open Credit Builder. Consider alternative secured cards that accept ITIN listed on our CreditCards page.</div></div>
                    <div class="rounded-xl border p-5"><div class="font-bold text-[15px]">Will I get a credit score immediately?</div><div class="text-[13px] text-slate-600 mt-2 leading-6">Most members see a first score within 30-45 days after first reporting, per Experian and Equifax timing. You need 6 months of history for FICO. Continue on-time payments.</div></div>
                    <div class="rounded-xl border p-5"><div class="font-bold text-[15px]">What is the approval odds 98%?</div><div class="text-[13px] text-slate-600 mt-2 leading-6">98% refers to eligible Chime members who meet direct deposit criteria. It is not a guaranteed approval from FICO perspective, but reflects no credit-check model. Source: Chime public disclosures and internal US member data.</div></div>
                </div>

